// A type has no parts to select, whether it is named bare or reached through
// a module: `Thing` declares no namespace `x` could come from, and that is
// the one mistake here. `x` names a field the type's own values carry, not a
// member the type itself declares, so [N-Variant] is what the resolver
// already said -- naming the qualifier's type as a second mistake describes
// the same line twice.
import pct

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    let _v = pct.Thing.x
    0
}
